  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Total expiring federal contract value in the next 12 months is $232B. NATIONAL TECHNOLOGY & ENGINEERING SOLUTIONS OF SANDIA, LLC holds the single largest expiring contract value at $42.8B. THE BOEING COMPANY appears twice on the top list with expiring contract values of $32B and $7.6B. SAVANNAH RIVER NUCLEAR SOLUTIONS LLC has $27.6B in expiring contract value. LOCKHEED MARTIN Services and corporate entries appear with $20.6B, $5B, and $4.6B entries, and NORTHROP GRUMMAN SYSTEMS CORPORATION and BATH IRON WORKS CORPORATION appear with $5.4B and $5B respectively. CHEMONICS INTERNATIONAL, INC. is on the list with $6.7B. Quarter-by-quarter, the largest expiring totals fall in Apr-Jun 2027 at $61B, followed by Jul-Sep 2026 at $52.9B, Oct-Dec 2026 at $42.7B, Jan-Mar 2027 at $40.3B, and Jul-Sep 2027 at $34.6B. Note. Award value figures are total contract values for contracts whose period of performance ends within the next 12 months. End dates can be extended by options and modifications.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which contractors hold the largest expiring contracts?",
        "body": "NATIONAL TECHNOLOGY & ENGINEERING SOLUTIONS OF SANDIA, LLC holds the largest expiring contract value at $42.8B. THE BOEING COMPANY holds $32B and a separate $7.6B expiring contract. SAVANNAH RIVER NUCLEAR SOLUTIONS LLC holds $27.6B, and LOCKHEED MARTIN SERVICES, LLC holds $20.6B. CHEMONICS INTERNATIONAL, INC., NORTHROP GRUMMAN SYSTEMS CORPORATION, LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION, and BATH IRON WORKS CORPORATION appear on the top list with $6.7B, $5.4B, $5B, and $5B respectively."
      },
      {
        "heading": "When do the largest expiring contracts end by quarter?",
        "body": "Apr-Jun 2027 has the largest expiring contract value at $61B. Jul-Sep 2026 has $52.9B, Oct-Dec 2026 has $42.7B, and Jan-Mar 2027 has $40.3B. Jul-Sep 2027 shows $34.6B in expiring contract value."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "Which large federal contracts are expiring soon?",
      "a": "Large federal contracts expiring soon include a $42.8B contract held by NATIONAL TECHNOLOGY & ENGINEERING SOLUTIONS OF SANDIA, LLC and a $32B contract held by THE BOEING COMPANY. Additional large expiring contracts include $27.6B for SAVANNAH RIVER NUCLEAR SOLUTIONS LLC, $20.6B for LOCKHEED MARTIN SERVICES, LLC, $7.6B and $32B entries for THE BOEING COMPANY, $6.7B for CHEMONICS INTERNATIONAL, INC., $5.4B for NORTHROP GRUMMAN SYSTEMS CORPORATION, $5B entries for LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION and BATH IRON WORKS CORPORATION, and a $4.6B entry for LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION."
    },
    {
      "q": "What is a contract recompete?",
      "a": "A contract recompete is the process agencies use to award a follow-on contract when a current contract is expiring. Agencies can run an open competition, limit competition, or extend the existing contract through options and modifications when determining the follow-on award."
    },
    {
      "q": "How current is this recompete data?",
      "a": "This recompete data covers contracts with periods of performance ending within the next 12 months and is reported for FY2026 to date. The data lists total contract values for those expiring contracts and notes that end dates can be extended by options and modifications."
    }
  ],
